{title: Seventy-Seven Times}
{subtitle: Matthew 18:21–22; Luke 15:11–32}
{key: G}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] |
| [G] | [D] | [Em] | [C] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Peter asked the Teacher on a dus[D]ty afternoon
[Em]How many times must I forgive my [C]brother, is seven times e[G]nough
Jesus looked him in the eye [D]and gave a gentle [Em]smile
Not seven times, my [C]friend, but sev-en-ty-sev-en times
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sev-en-ty-[G]sev-en times and then a [D]little more
Leave the light [Em]on in the window, keep a key [C]beneath the door
'Cause the [G]grace I've been given is the grace [D]I'm meant to give
Sev-en-ty-[Em]sev-en times, [C]that's the way I want to [G]live
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There's a boy who took his money and he [D]ran off to the town
[Em]Spent it all on easy living till the [C]money ran out
[G]He came walking home in rags, re[D]hearsing what he'd say
[Em]But his father saw him coming from a [C]long, long way
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [G] | [D] | [Em] | [C] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
He ran [D]to him and held him tight
[C]Threw a party on that night
[D]He was lost and now he's [C]found
He was dead and he's a[G]live
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Sev-en-ty-[D]sev-en times [Em]
[C]That's the way I want to [G]live
{end_of_verse}

